"text": "The unit, integration and CI-script entries are /implement's. The session-binary smoke covers the boot path. The change adds a stand function and touches no existing boot (`boot`, `boot_timer`, `boot_cells`, `boot_load` and the session host are unchanged), so the smoke reads the six served tasks unmoved. No live leg: the cold-agent live run stays «Cold-agent bar»'s and is never fired here. Three one-shot controls are /implement's, each fired as `gate.py control` with its lines in `.andromeda/cache/chunks/2026-11-17-a-component-in-isolation/evidence/`, and none is an entry. (a) Entry 3, file `packages/blitz-test-harness/src/harness.rs`: the edit removes the named-child mount, step 1's `VComponent::new` child, so the component becomes the vdom root (the exact text is recorded in the evidence when the code stands). The case is the TaskShell-props test, filtered by its name. `--timeout 900`; a `timeout` reading is no hold. (b) Entry 3, file `examples/seven_guis/src/stand.rs`: the edit removes step 2's `TimerTicks` root context. The case is the Timer-alone test, filtered by its name. `--timeout 900`. (c) Entry 1, file `packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/boundary.rs`: the edit removes `contexts.insert(0, root.clone());`. The case is the fallback test by its name. `--timeout 600`. Each reads that case `failed`, then green restored. The guard entry reads that no carrier moved, against HEAD at P4. The operator pass fires the hygiene entry, the push and the CI read. A CI run must witness the stand check on windows and macOS, which the matrix runs; that diff is not OS-sensitive."
}
],
